221 1 1 1 true 2 | 1 11 2 1 7 | 1 0 | `rival`'s `Owned` rows are not replaced and stand as they were — `Owned` row 0 is `mirror`'s and a write names it `rival`'s — a row has one owner from its first write: key it by what distinguishes its writers | `looping`'s `Loose` rows are not replaced and stand as they were — a `Loose` write moved the whole relation while a query (reader 3), which read it this revision, is still running — a query settles on one state of what it read | a `@query` wrote a row with no owner — a query answers, it writes no rows of its own; hand the rows to a named owner (`Rel.replaced(db, owner, rows)`)
